        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Presented in excellent condition throughout, this spacious three/four-bedroom semi-detached family home enjoys a peaceful position within a quiet, low-density development close to Mullingar Regional Hospital, the town centre and the N4 motorway. Offering bright accommodation, generous outdoor space and a superb location, this attractive home is ideal for families, first-time buyers or those seeking convenient access to local amenities and commuter routes.\n\nThe accommodation comprises of an entrance hall with under-stairs storage, decorative coving and quality flooring throughout. To the front of the property, the spacious sitting room is filled with natural light from a large bay window and features a solid fuel fireplace. A second reception room offers excellent flexibility as an additional family room, home office or fourth bedroom. To the rear, the open-plan kitchen and dining area is fitted with an extensive range of wall and floor units, integrated cooking appliances and direct access to the rear garden through sliding patio doors. A separate utility room provides further storage, while a fully tiled ground floor wet room adds practicality and convenience.\n\nUpstairs, there are three generously proportioned bedrooms, all with built-in wardrobes, with the primary bedroom coming en-suite. A well-appointed family bathroom completes the first-floor accommodation.\n\nExternally, the property occupies a desirable corner site with beautifully maintained lawns to the front and rear. The sunny rear garden features a paved patio area, while a gated side entrance provides easy access. Ample off-street parking is available to the front, and the property enjoys an attractive setting with green areas to the side and rear.\n\nIdeally located within walking distance of St. Finian's College, Mullingar Regional Hospital and a host of local amenities, this superb home also enjoys easy access to Mullingar town centre, the N4 motorway and nearby Lough Owel.\n\nThis impressive family home is ready for immediate occupation. Early viewing is highly recommended.\n\nAccommodation\nEntrance Hall 2.099m x 2.026m (6'11\" x 6'8\"):\nCoving, laminate flooring, ceiling rose, understairs storage, carpet stairs.\n\nSitting Room 4.569m x 3.593m (15' x 11'9\"):\nLaminate flooring, coving, TV point, solid fuel fireplace, bay window.\n\nLiving Room 2.656m x 4.503m (8'9\" x 14'9\"):\nFront aspect, laminate flooring.\n\nKitchen/Dining Area\n5.825m x 3.360m (19'1\" x 11'):\nFitted wall and floor units, hob with extractor fan, tiled flooring, sink, sliding patio door to rear, TV point.\n\nUtility Room 2.64m x 2.645m (8'8\" x 8'8\"):\nTiled floor, door to rear, plumbing for washer/dryer, fridge, door to rear.\n\nWet Room 0.793m x 2.628m (2'7\" x 8'7\"):\nTiled flooring, WC, wash hand basin, towel rail, mirror, fan, shower cubicle with Triton T80 unit.\n\nLanding 1.944m x 3.739m (6'5\" x 12'3\"):\nCarpet flooring, access to attic, hotpress, coving.\n\nBedroom One 3.62m x 3.112m (11'11\" x 10'3\"):\nWooden flooring, rear aspect, double room, built in wardrobes.\n\nBathroom 2.116m x 1.911m (6'11\" x 6'3\"):\nTowel rail, tiled flooring, bath, wall tiling, mirror, WC, wash hand basin.\n\nBedroom Two 2.522m x 2.358m (8'3\" x 7'9\"):\nWooden flooring, built in wardrobes, front aspect.\n\nBedroom Three 3.778m x 4.128m (12'5\" x 13'7\"): Wooden flooring, front aspect, TV point, built in wardrobes, coving.\n\nEn-Suite 2.939m x 0.805m (9'8\" x 2'8\"):\nTiled flooring, wall tiling, WC, wash hand basin, towel rail, shower cubicle with triton T90 unit, extractor fan.\n\nSpecial Features & Services\n• 3/4-bedroom semi-detached family home\n• Quiet low-density cul-de-sac location\n• Flexible second reception room or fourth bedroom\n• Bright open-plan kitchen and dining area\n• Ground floor wet room\n• Built-in wardrobes in all bedrooms\n• Upstairs floors sanded 2026\n• Oil-fired central heating\n• Double-glazed windows and doors\n• Beautifully maintained gardens\n• Sunny rear garden with paved patio area\n• Corner site\n• Gated side access\n• Ample off-street parking\n• Freshly painted throughout\n• Ground floor floors sanded in 2025\n• Green areas to the side and rear\n• Short walk to St. Finian's College\n• Minutes from Mullingar Regional Hospital\n• Close to Lough Owel\n• Easy access to Mullingar town centre and the N4 motorway\n• Close to bus stop for M4 direct bus service to Dublin and Mullingar's local link service (both bus stops st hospital).\n\nIncluded\n• Fixtures\n• Fittings\n• Light fittings\n• Blinds\n• Oven/hob"
      },
